## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason with 128-bit data layout and perform blockwise rearrangements using only bitwise ops. It also checks handling of multi-word operands without branching.

## Key Concepts

- Block masking and extraction
- Cross-word recombination
- Branchless 128-bit manipulation

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;

uint128 swapAdjacentBlocks128(uint128 x, unsigned block) {
    uint64_t M = (1ULL << block) - 1;
    uint64_t A0 = x.lo & M;
    uint64_t A1 = (x.lo >> block) & M;
    uint64_t A2 = x.hi & M;
    uint64_t A3 = (x.hi >> block) & M;
    uint64_t loP = (A0 << block) | A1;
    uint64_t hiP = (A2 << block) | A3;
    return (uint128){.hi = hiP, .lo = loP};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend to non-uniform block counts or dynamic block that isn't divisor of 128?
- How to optimize for block=16 across many values in tight loops?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to derive circular adjacency via rotation, and to implement a 128-bit popcount using SWAR style reductions; ensures understanding of cross-boundary bit relationships.

## Key Concepts

- Circular adjacency using ROTL
- 128-bit representation as two 64-bit halves
- SWAR/popcount with bitwise masks and shifts

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;

static inline uint128 rotl128(uint128 x){
  uint128 r;
  r.hi = (x.hi << 1) | (x.lo >> 63);
  r.lo = (x.lo << 1) | (x.hi >> 63);
  return r;
}

static inline unsigned int popcount128(uint128 x){
  uint64_t a = x.hi;
  uint64_t b = x.lo;
  a = a - ((a >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  a = (a & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((a >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  a = (a + (a >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  unsigned int ca = (a * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;

  b = b - ((b >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  b = (b & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((b >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  b = (b + (b >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  unsigned int cb = (b * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;

  return ca + cb;
}
```

